TI  - Isolation and characterization of seven tetrarepeat microsatellite loci in the indo-pacific finless porpoise (neophocaena phocaenoides) and their amplification across cetacean species
T2  - Collection and Research
LA  - English
KW  - /unread
AB  - The Indo-Pacific finless porpoise (Neophocaena phocaenoides) inhabits a narrow band of shallow waters along the coastal Indo-Pacific and experiences high levels of incidental mortality due to fishery activities. We isolated seven polymorphic microsatellite loci with (GAAA)n motifs from finless porpoises using an enrichment cloning procedure. We characterized these loci by screening 32 finless porpoises from the Taiwan Strait. The mean number of alleles per locus was 10.3 (range 5~16). The observed heterozygosity of each locus ranged 0.3~0.9. Evaluation of cross-species amplification of these markers across 14 cetaceans in five families indicated that these microsatellite loci are useful for ecological, evolutionary, and conservative research on the finless porpoise, as well as other cetacean species.
