TI  - Occurrence, distribution and ecological risk assessment of phthalate esters in sediments of poyang lake and its tributaries
T2  - Water, Air, & Soil Pollution
LA  - English
KW  - /unread
AB  - Occurrence, spatial distribution, influencing factors and ecological risks of 15 Phthalate esters (PAEs) in the sediments of Poyang Lake and its tributaries were investigated. The concentrations of total PAEs (Σ15 PAEs) in the sediments of Poyang Lake ranged from 9.8 to 3765.6 ng/g dry weight and Σ15 PAEs of the tributaries ranged from 32.7 to 590.9 ng/g. Di-(2-ethylhexyl) phthalate was the dominant PAE in the sediments of Poyang Lake, which accounted for approximately half of the Σ15 PAEs.
