TI  - A review of legal and policy framework for sustainable management of marine living resources in bangladeshi waters
LA  - English
KW  - /unread
AB  - The coastal and marine waters of Bangladesh are bestowed with distinctive and enriched biodiversity, located in the north-eastern tip of the Bay of Bengal. These diverse biological resources create a great opportunity for the nation to get the invaluable ecosystem services. However, despite existing policies, rules and regulations and the related institutions in the country, these resources face multi-dimensional challenges in the natural environment. The present study has investigated the current legal and policy frameworks of Bangladesh for the protection and conservation of biological resources in the coastal and marine waters of the country and pointed out some major gaps and challenges in the governance system. The findings indicated that the core legal frameworks are more concerned with monitoring and surveillance, while less focusing on the science-based and community-engaged ecosystem approach to sustainable management. The results also identified some gaps in the governance system, which includes inefficiency in monitoring, control, and surveillance (MCS) due to inadequate funds for logistics, lack of trained personnel, insufficient coordination among related institutions, and non-functioning of the Joint Monitoring Cell in the country. The results showed the inefficiency in the management of the Marine Protected Areas (MPAs) in the country. The investigations also identified that overfishing, destructive fishing, climate change, anthropogenic pollution, IUU fishing, and the social and poor economic conditions of the fisherfolk are the major reasons for the biodiversity degradation in the Bay of Bengal. This research suggested that addressing the gaps to strengthen the policy framework and creating a science-based integrated coastal and marine biodiversity policy, elucidating the proper institutional mandates and engaging all stakeholders, would significantly amplify governance effectiveness in the country.
